WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Leading a Waldorf school today asks a great deal of us.

00:04.000 --> 00:07.000
We're holding a rich educational tradition

00:07.000 --> 00:12.000
while responding to a world that is changing remarkably quickly.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.000
I'm Karen Atkinson, and for more than 30 years

00:15.000 --> 00:18.000
I've worked with Waldorf education as a teacher,

00:18.000 --> 00:23.000
a mentor, pedagogical leader, coach, and consultant.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.000
What those years have taught me

00:25.000 --> 00:30.000
is a healthy school isn't created by having all the answers.

00:30.000 --> 00:34.000
They grow when people have the courage and the space

00:34.000 --> 00:36.000
to ask the right questions.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.000
That's where my work begins:

00:38.000 --> 00:42.000
listening carefully, uncovering patterns,

00:42.000 --> 00:44.000
clarifying what matters,

00:44.000 --> 00:48.000
and finding practical ways to move forward together.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.000
If your school is at a point of change,

00:52.000 --> 00:57.500
challenge, or possibility, let's begin there together.
